<title>USA: Triton Ecuador Huataracu-1 well uneconomic.</title>
<headline>Triton Ecuador Huataracu-1 well uneconomic.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Triton Energy Ltd said Friday the Huataracu-1 well on Block 19 in Ecuador's Oriente Basin has been plugged and abandoned.  Multiple tests in the well resulted in the recovery of uneconomic volumes of oil, it said.</p>
<p>Triton said it and its partners continue to evaluate remaining opportunities on the block.</p>
<p>Triton is the operator of Block 19 with a 55 percent working interest. Partners are Vintage Petroleum Inc with 30 percent and Ranger Oil Ltd with 15 percent.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.))</p>
</text>
